{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And a quickening of raw flesh.</b> שינמי\"נט בְּלַעַ\"ז — that part of the white within the swelling turns to the appearance of flesh; this too is a sign of impurity — white hair without a quickening, and a quickening without white hair — and even though מִחְיָה is stated only regarding the swelling, in all the appearances and their offshoots it is a sign of impurity."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The la'az שינמי\"נט is Old French s'enmenit / s'envertit, 'it turns greenish,' i.e., takes on a raw-flesh hue."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:07.540800577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}